le-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">shredded lettuce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for crunch and freshness</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">piece</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">carrot</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">julienned for added texture</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">piece</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">cucumber</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">julienned for a refreshing crunch</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh mint leaves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds a burst of flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh cilantro leaves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for aromatic notes</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">hoisin-peanut dipping sauce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for delicious dipping</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-3392-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3392\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 large shallow dish&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For soaking rice paper wrappers</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 clean work surface&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For assembling the rolls</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-3392-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-3392-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"3392\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Fill a large shallow dish with warm water.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Dip one rice paper wrapper in the warm water for about 5 seconds. Place it on a clean work surface.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Arrange 2 shrimp halves in a row on the lower third of the wrapper.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Top the shrimp with a small handful of vermicelli, lettuce, carrot, cucumber, mint, and cilantro.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Fold the bottom edge of the wrapper over the filling. Then fold in both sides and roll tightly to seal.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Repeat the process with the remaining wrappers and fillings.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-3392-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Serve immediately with hoisin-peanut dipping sauce. Enjoy your delicious shrimp spring rolls!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-3392-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>5g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>25g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these fresh ingredients to create delicious shrimp spring rolls!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls.webp\" alt=\"A variety of fresh ingredients for shrimp spring rolls displayed on a wooden kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-3390\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>8 rice paper wrappers</strong> – for wrapping the rolls</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>16 cooked shrimp</strong> – halved lengthwise</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>4 oz rice vermicelli noodles</strong> – cooked and drained</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup shredded lettuce</strong> – for crunch and freshness</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 carrot</strong> – julienned for added texture</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cucumber</strong> – julienned for a refreshing crunch</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup fresh mint leaves</strong> – adds a burst of flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup fresh cilantro leaves</strong> – for aromatic notes</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 cup hoisin-peanut dipping sauce</strong> – for delicious dipping</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-shrimp-spring-rolls\"><strong>How to Make shrimp spring rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making shrimp spring rolls is a delightful experience! The preparation time is about 20 minutes, with no cooking time required. Just a little extra time for assembling, and you’ll have a fresh, tasty treat ready to enjoy!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making shrimp spring rolls, including filling a dish with water, dipping a rice paper wrapper, adding shrimp and vegetables, and rolling the spring rolls.\" class=\"wp-image-3391\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Step-by-Step-Shrimp-Spring-Rolls-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Fill the Dish</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fill a large shallow dish with warm water.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Dip the Wrapper</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Dip one rice paper wrapper in the warm water for about 5 seconds. Place it on a clean work surface.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add the Shrimp</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Arrange 2 shrimp halves in a row on the lower third of the wrapper.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Layer the Veggies</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Top the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrimp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">shrimp </a>with a small handful of vermicelli, lettuce, carrot, cucumber, mint, and cilantro.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Roll It Up</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fold the bottom edge of the wrapper over the filling. Then fold in both sides and roll tightly to seal.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Repeat</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Repeat the process with the remaining wrappers and fillings.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Serve immediately with hoisin-peanut dipping sauce. Enjoy your delicious shrimp spring rolls!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Appetizer</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Vietnamese</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Low-calorie</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Fresh with dipping sauce</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-shrimp-spring-rolls\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making shrimp spring rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Soak rice paper in warm water just until pliable, not too soft.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use fresh herbs like mint and cilantro for vibrant flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t overfill the rolls; keep it simple for easier wrapping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a homemade dipping sauce for a personal touch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Practice rolling with a few test sheets to perfect your technique.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-shrimp-spring-rolls\"><strong>How to Serve this shrimp spring rolls</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with a zesty peanut dipping sauce for a nutty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a sweet chili sauce for a delightful contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy alongside a fresh cucumber salad for a refreshing crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with fresh herbs like mint or cilantro for added flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a side of pickled vegetables for a tangy twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve on a platter with colorful veggies for a vibrant presentation.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to keep your shrimp spring rolls fresh and delicious:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Place leftover <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_roll\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">spring rolls</a> in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Separate layers with parchment paper to prevent sticking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap each spring roll tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped rolls in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For best results, reheat in an oven at 350°F (175°C) for 10-15 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Alternatively, use an air fryer for 5-7 minutes until crispy.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwaving is quick but may make them soggy; use a paper towel to absorb moisture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What goes into a shrimp spring roll?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Shrimp spring rolls typically include fresh shrimp, rice paper wrappers, and a variety of fresh vegetables such as lettuce, carrots, and cucumbers. You can also add herbs like mint or cilantro for extra flavor. The combination of these ingredients creates a refreshing and delicious bite!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What ingredients go in a spring roll?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>In addition to shrimp, spring rolls can include a mix of vegetables like bell peppers, bean sprouts, and avocado. You can also use vermicelli noodles for added texture. The key is to use fresh, crisp ingredients that complement each other well, making each roll a delightful experience!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Are shrimp spring rolls healthy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, shrimp spring rolls can be a healthy option! They are typically low in calories and packed with nutrients from the fresh vegetables. Using lean shrimp and minimal oil for cooking keeps them light. Just be mindful of the dipping sauces, as they can add extra calories. Enjoying them in moderation is key!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What&#8217;s the difference between Chinese egg roll and spring roll?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The main difference lies in the wrappers and fillings. Egg rolls have a thicker, crispy wrapper made with egg, while spring rolls use a thinner rice paper or wheat wrapper. Additionally, egg rolls are often filled with a mixture of meat and vegetables, while spring rolls are usually lighter, focusing on fresh vegetables and shrimp. Both are delicious in their own right!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making shrimp spring rolls at home is not just a recipe; it’s a delightful experience! Picture yourself rolling up fresh ingredients, feeling the crunch of the veggies, and savoring that juicy shrimp. It’s simple, fun, and oh-so-rewarding! So gather your loved ones, whip up a batch, and enjoy these tasty bites together. You’ve got this!</p>\n",
